
<a name=30.00><b>1994 FIFA World Cup Qualifying Teams</b></a>
<p>
    Argentina  --  The Argentines, seeded No. 1 in Group 'D,'  have participated in 10
of the 14 World Cup tournaments (1930-1934, 1958-1966, 1974-1990).  Argentina hosted
the finals in 1978, winning the World Cup trophy that year, and won it again in 1986.  It
was the runner-up at the first World Cup tournament in 1930, and again at the last one
in 1990.  In its 48 World Cup games played, Argentina has 24 wins, nine draws and 15
losses.
<p>
    Belgium  --  The Belgians, seeded No. 1 in Group 'F,' have taken part in eight
World Cups (1930-1938, 1954, 1970, 1982-1990).  Their best finish was fourth place in
the 1986 Mexico World Cup, losing 4-2 to France in the consolation game.  In its 25
matches played, Belgium has seven wins, four draws and 14 losses.
<p>
     Bolivia  --  The Bolivians, in Group 'C,' have played in just two World Cup finals
(1930, 1950).  They have lost all three games in which they have played by scores of 0-4,
0-4, 0-8, but are looking for improvement in 1994.
<p>
    Brazil  --  The Brazilians, seeded No. 1 in Group 'B,' have more success than any
other nation in the World Cup, qualifying for all 14 (1930-1990).  Brazil was the first
country to win three World Cup trophies (1958, 1962, 1970), and was the runner-up in
1950, the year it hosted the tournament.  In its 66 games, Brazil has compiled an
enviable record of 44 wins, 11 draws and 11 losses, outscoring the opposition by 148
goals to 65.
<p>
    Bulgaria  --  The Bulgarians, in Group 'D,' have participated in five World Cup
finals (1962-1974, 1986).  They are still seeking their first World Cup victory, having
compiled a record of no wins, six draws and 10 losses.
<p>
    Cameroon  --  Cameroon, in Group 'B,' has a brief World Cup history, having
qualified for two tournaments (1982, 1990).  Its best finish was a 3-2 quarterfinal loss to
England in 1990, with all three of England's goals coming on penalty kicks.  In its eight
World Cup games, Cameroon has a combined record of three wins, three draws and two
losses.
<p>
    Colombia  --  The Colombians, in Group 'A,' have taken part in two World Cup
finals (1962, 1990).  Their best finish was a 2-1 loss to Cameroon in the second round
in 1990.  In its seven World Cup games, the South American team has a World Cup
record of one win, two draws and four losses.
<p>
    Germany  --  The defending champion, the Germans, seeded No. 1 in Group 'C,'
have appeared in 12 of the 14 World Cups (1934-1938, 1954-1990).  Germany is one of
only three countries to win three World Cup trophies (1954, 1974, 1990).  Brazil and Italy
are the other two.  Having played as "West" Germany until this World Cup, the champs
have an impressive World Cup history.  In its 68 World Cup games, Germany has 39
wins, 15 draws and 14 losses, and has outscored its opposition by 145 goals to 90.  In
the last five World Cups, Germany has won twice (1974, 1990), and been the runner-up
in two others (1982, 1986).
<p>
    Greece  --  When Greece, in Group 'D,' tied Russia, 1-1, in a qualifying game on
May 23, 1993, it marked the first time the European nation had qualified for the World
Cup finals.
<p>
    Ireland (The Republic of)  --  The Irish, in Group 'E,' are playing in only their
second World Cup, also having qualified for the 1990 finals.  But Ireland made the best
of its one and only World Cup, making it to the quarterfinals (despite not winning a single
game) before losing, 1-0, to the host Italians.  In its five World Cup games, Ireland has
no wins, four draws and one loss.
<p>
    Italy  --  Italy, seeded No. 1 in Group 'E,' is one of only three nations to win three
World Cup titles (1934, 1938, 1982).  Brazil and Germany are the other two. In addition,
Italy was the runner-up in 1970.  Italy has participated in 12 of the 14 World Cup finals
(1934-1954, 1962-1990), hosting the 1990 finals.  Its outstanding World Cup record
includes 54 matches, with 31 wins, 12 draws and 11 losses.
<p>
    Korea Republic  --  The Republic of Korea, also known as South Korea, is drawn
in Group 'C' and is appearing in its fourth World Cup finals, having qualified in 1954, 1986
and 1990.  It has not registered a victory in eight World Cup games, drawing one and
losing the other seven.
<p>
    Mexico  --  Mexico, in Group 'E,' has appeared in nine World Cup tournaments
(1930, 1950-1970, 1978, 1986).  It is the only nation to host two World Cup finals (1970,
1986).  Mexico's best finish was the quarterfinals in both 1970 and 1986 (the years it
served as host).  In 1970 Mexico lost, 4-1, to Italy in the quarters, and in 1986 it drew
with West Germany, 0-0, but lost 4-1 on penalty kicks.  Its World Cup record includes six
wins, six draws and 17 losses.
<p>
    Morocco  --  Morocco, in Group 'F,' is playing in its third World Cup, having
qualified in 1970 and 1986.  Its best finish was the second round in 1986, when it lost 1-0
to eventual runner-up West Germany.  Morocco's World Cup record includes one win,
three draws and three losses.
<p>
    The Netherlands  --  Often referred to as Holland, the tiny European nation has
participated in five World Cups (1934-1938, 1974-1978, 1990).  Drawn in Group 'F,' the
Netherlands has never won the World Cup, but has finished second twice (1974, 1978). 
In 1974, it lost, 2-1, to West Germany, and in 1978 it dropped the championship game,
3-1, to Argentina.  Holland's World Cup record includes eight wins, six draws and six
losses.
<p>
    Nigeria  --  Nigeria, in Group 'D,' is one of three countries playing in its first World
Cup (the others are Greece and Saudi Arabia), and one of four if you count Russia, which
played previously as a part of the Soviet Union.
<p>
    Norway  --  The Norwegians, in Group 'E,' are participating in only their second
World Cup tournament, the other in 1938, when they lost their one and only game, 2-1,
to the eventual champion, Italy.
<p>
    Romania  --  The Romanians, in Group 'A,' have taken part in five World Cup
finals (1930-1938, 1970, 1990).  Romania's best finish was a 1990 second-round loss to
the Republic of Ireland, 0-0 in regulation, and then 5-4 on penalty kicks.  Its combined
World Cup record is three wins, three draws and six losses.
<p>
    Russia  --  As Russia, this team has not competed in the World Cup, although as
part of the Soviet Union it had a hand in seven finals.  Drawn in Group 'B,' Russia has
most of the top talent from the former Soviet Union team.  The Soviet Union compiled a
World Cup record of 15 wins, six draws and 10 losses, making it to the semifinals in
1966, losing, 2-1, to Portugal.
<p>
    Saudi Arabia  --  The Saudis, in Group 'F,' are participating in their first World Cup
tournament, qualifying as one of two entries from the Asian group.
<p>
    Spain  --  The Spanish, in Group 'C,' have participated in eight World Cup
tournaments (1934, 1950, 1962-1966, 1978-1990).  Spain served as host for the 1982
World Cup.  Its best finish was a quarterfinal loss to Belgium in 1986, 1-1 and 5-4 on
penalty kicks.  Spain's World Cup record includes 13 wins, seven draws and 12 losses.
<p>
    Sweden  --  The Swedes, in Group 'B,' have taken part in eight World Cups (1934-
1950, 1958, 1970-1978, 1990).  Sweden served as host of the tournament in 1958, and
had its best World Cup then, earning runner-up honors to Brazil, losing 5-2 in the final. 
In its 31 World Cup games, Sweden has 11 wins, six draws and 14 losses.
<p>
    Switzerland  --  The Swiss, in Group 'A,' have appeared in six World Cup
tournaments, but have not participated in 28 years (1934-1954, 1962-1966). 
Switzerland's best World Cup finish was a 7-5 quarterfinal loss to Austria in 1954, when
it served as the host nation.  Its World Cup record includes five wins, two draws and 11
losses.
<p>
    United States  --  The U.S., seeded No. 1 in Group 'A,' has participated in four
other World Cups (1930-1934, 1950, 1990).  The best finish by a U.S. team in World Cup
play was third place in the first tournament in 1930, where it dropped a 6-1 decision to
eventual runner-up Argentina.  In its 1950 appearance, the U.S. enjoyed its most
celebrated World Cup moment with a 1-0 upset win over England.  Its tournament record
includes three wins, no draws and seven losses.

